      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-296230",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/48/48a59cdc092ef2cb25220bb00262ebd79f068a4bf79aa643599eddc42979cd3b.png)\n\nThe manager of a bookstore kept track of how many books each of their regular customers purchased during two different months. This information is displayed using the box plots shown above.\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe interquartile range (IQR) of the first month's purchases is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nThe interquartile range (IQR) of the second month's purchases is\n{{field-2}}.\n\nComparing the IQRs suggests that the data for the {{field-3}}\nmonth is more spread out."
